# Mutations for FloatLock. Each names the one property that must fail on it and
# runs only where that property holds on the unmutated spec.

mutation the caps check ignores what earlier turns committed
detects CapHolds
only base refills=3
- /\ IF ~live \/ Committed + Price > Cap
+ /\ IF ~live \/ Price > Cap

mutation the reservation never lands, so the next caps read misses it
detects CapHolds
only base refills=3
- /\ visible' = [visible EXCEPT ![r] = TRUE]
-                     /\ Say(r, "ok")
+ /\ UNCHANGED visible
+                     /\ Say(r, "ok")

mutation the top-up row is not written before the send
detects MovedRecorded
only money refills=2
- /\ topUp' = [topUp EXCEPT ![r] = 1]
+ /\ UNCHANGED topUp

mutation the refill skips the live check and writes the top-up ahead on an ended connection
detects NoSendAfterEnd
only base refills=1 disc=1
- /\ IF ~live \/ Committed + Price > Cap
-                  THEN Leave(r, "refused")
-                  ELSE Go(r, "assert212") /\ UNCHANGED outcome
-             /\ UNCHANGED <<funded, lock, db, chain>>
-
- \* hold.assertHeld() (218), then ensurePayerFunds sends only when the payer is short.
- Assert212(r) == /\ pc[r] = "assert212"
-                 /\ IF lost[r]
-                      THEN Leave(r, "error")
-                      ELSE (Go(r, "addTopUp") \/ Go(r, "skip")) /\ UNCHANGED outcome
-                 /\ UNCHANGED <<funded, lock, db, chain>>
-
- \* owns() then writeTopUpAhead in one tx before the send (110-113,
- \* store.ts:233). Not owning throws FloatLost, and on an ended connection the
- \* write-ahead throws: either way nothing is sent and the turn ends in error.
- AddTopUp(r) == /\ pc[r] = "addTopUp"
-                /\ IF Owns(r) /\ live
+ /\ IF Committed + Price > Cap
+                  THEN Leave(r, "refused")
+                  ELSE Go(r, "assert212") /\ UNCHANGED outcome
+             /\ UNCHANGED <<funded, lock, db, chain>>
+
+ \* hold.assertHeld() (218), then ensurePayerFunds sends only when the payer is short.
+ Assert212(r) == /\ pc[r] = "assert212"
+                 /\ IF lost[r]
+                      THEN Leave(r, "error")
+                      ELSE (Go(r, "addTopUp") \/ Go(r, "skip")) /\ UNCHANGED outcome
+                 /\ UNCHANGED <<funded, lock, db, chain>>
+
+ \* owns() then writeTopUpAhead in one tx before the send (110-113,
+ \* store.ts:233). Not owning throws FloatLost, and on an ended connection the
+ \* write-ahead throws: either way nothing is sent and the turn ends in error.
+ AddTopUp(r) == /\ pc[r] = "addTopUp"
+                /\ IF Owns(r)

mutation the catch drops the funded outcome when the reserve tx fails
detects MovedReachesCaller
only money refills=2
- /\ outcome' = [outcome EXCEPT ![r] = IF funded[r] THEN "funding_failed" ELSE "error"]
+ /\ outcome' = [outcome EXCEPT ![r] = "error"]

mutation the catch returns funded as ok when the reserve tx fails, so the caller signs unreserved
detects CapHolds
only cap refills=3 txfault
- /\ outcome' = [outcome EXCEPT ![r] = IF funded[r] THEN "funding_failed" ELSE "error"]
+ /\ outcome' = [outcome EXCEPT ![r] = IF funded[r] THEN Returned(r) ELSE "error"]

mutation the session end keeps the lock and the wait has no lock_timeout
detects WaitEnds
only base refills=2
- Free(t) == IF lockOwner = t THEN None ELSE lockOwner
- GiveUp(t) == /\ pc[t] = "wait"
+ Free(t) == lockOwner
+ GiveUp(t) == /\ FALSE /\ pc[t] = "wait"

mutation a dropped session keeps the lock on the server
detects reach:LockStolen
- /\ lockOwner' = Free(t)
-            /\ drops' = drops + 1
+ /\ UNCHANGED lockOwner
+            /\ drops' = drops + 1

mutation onclose never sets lost
detects reach:LostSeen
- /\ lost' = [lost EXCEPT ![t] = TRUE]
+ /\ UNCHANGED lost

mutation a disconnect never ends the connection
detects reach:Ended
- /\ live' = FALSE
-           /\ Leave(d, "ok")
+ /\ UNCHANGED live
+           /\ Leave(d, "ok")

mutation addTopUp adds the amount twice
detects TypeOK
only base refills=1
- /\ topUp' = [topUp EXCEPT ![r] = 1]
+ /\ topUp' = [topUp EXCEPT ![r] = 2]

mutation a send that throws after the bundler took it reports a plain refusal
detects MovedReachesCaller
only money refills=1 lostreply
- /\ Land(r)
-                  /\ Leave(r, "funding_failed")
+ /\ Land(r)
+                  /\ Leave(r, "refused")

mutation the reserve tx does not check the fence, as before it existed
detects CapHolds
only cap refills=3 drops=1
- Owns(r) == ~lost[r] /\ took[r] = fence
+ Owns(r) == ~lost[r]

mutation the top-up write does not check the fence
detects NoStaleTopUp
only cap refills=3 drops=1
- /\ IF Owns(r) /\ live
+ /\ IF live

mutation an end does not wait for a top-up in flight
detects NoSendAfterEnd
only end refills=1 disc=1 drops=1
- /\ ~InFlight
-           /\ live' = FALSE
+ /\ live' = FALSE

mutation the top-up is written ahead whether or not the connection is live
detects NoSendAfterEnd
only end refills=1 disc=1 drops=1
- /\ IF Owns(r) /\ live
+ /\ IF Owns(r)

mutation revokeByGrant ends past its deadline under a top-up in flight
detects NoSendAfterEnd
only end refills=1 revoke=1
- /\ lockOwner # None
-                /\ ~InFlight
+ /\ lockOwner # None

mutation fit counts what moved on chain and ignores the open rows
detects ExecCapHolds
only exec execs=2 drops=0
- /\ IF (IF pinned[e] THEN snap[e] ELSE ExecSpent) + Cardinality(pend[e]) + 1 > ExecCap
+ /\ IF (IF pinned[e] THEN snap[e] ELSE ExecSpent) + 1 > ExecCap

mutation the execute records its rows without owns(), after another turn took the lock
detects ExecCapHolds
only exec execs=2 drops=1
- /\ IF Owns(e)
+ /\ IF TRUE

mutation a row is released while its userOp may still land, as a block window running out would
detects ExecCapHolds
only exec execs=2 drops=0
- /\ op[e] \in {"landed", "reverted"}
+ /\ op[e] \in {"sent", "landed", "reverted"}

mutation the execute sends with no row recorded
detects ExecRecorded
only exec execs=2 drops=0
- /\ row' = [row EXCEPT ![e] = "open"]
+ /\ UNCHANGED row

mutation fit counts as held a run the pinned read already has, the double count
detects CountedOnce
only exec execs=2 drops=0
- /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![e] = {x \in Execs : row[x] \in {"open", "landed"} /\ x \notin seen[e]}]
+ /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![e] = {x \in Execs : row[x] \in {"open", "landed"}}]

mutation held counts open rows only, so a run its receipt landed after the read counts nowhere
detects ExecCapHolds
only exec execs=2 drops=0
- /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![e] = {x \in Execs : row[x] \in {"open", "landed"} /\ x \notin seen[e]}]
+ /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![e] = {x \in Execs : row[x] = "open" /\ x \notin seen[e]}]

mutation the record tx skips the live check, so an end between the checks and the record is missed
detects NoExecAfterEnd
only exec execs=1 revoke=1
- /\ IF Owns(e) /\ live
+ /\ IF Owns(e)

mutation an end ignores an execute recorded and not yet submitted
detects NoExecAfterEnd
only exec execs=2 disc=1 drops=1
- InFlight == (\E r \in Refills : topUp[r] = 1 /\ ~visible[r] /\ pc[r] # "done") \/ ExecInFlight
+ InFlight == (\E r \in Refills : topUp[r] = 1 /\ ~visible[r] /\ pc[r] # "done")
